It is a misperception that there is some advantage
to carrying goodies so as to be able to ID them
immediately as a ?oID appears. Don't do that. Create
a stash, using a box, bag, or chest dragged to the
top of some stairs you are about to descend, to make
it easy to recognize (name the container, too), put
everything not of immediate use in it, including
particularly all unIDed stuff that is too dangerous
to ID by using it. The chest won't go away [though
an overambitious warhorse or similar pet may play
keep-away with it for a while]. You then have every
right to come back when you find more ID scrolls,
loot the container and ID the stuff at last.

